  "purpose": "Evidence layer for the benchmark-aware router. SKILL.md carries only the derived compact rules; this file carries the records those rules were derived from, with enough methodology to tell comparable numbers from incomparable ones. Nothing reads this file at runtime -- it is read when a rule is questioned or re-derived.",
  "rules_of_use": [
    "Two numbers are comparable only when benchmark, benchmark_version, harness, tool_access, agent_scaffold and effort match, AND they share a comparability_group. Otherwise they are 'not directly comparable' -- say so instead of ranking them.",
    "Never interpolate a score between effort levels. A missing rung is null, not an estimate.",
    "null means 'not published'. It is never a placeholder for a guess.",
    "A vendor-run row that measures a competitor (source_tier A, vendor_run true) is direction evidence, not a settled ranking. Triangulate with an independent row before it decides anything.",
    "An aggregate index never overrides a task-specific benchmark for a task that benchmark covers."
  ],
  "source_tiers": {
    "A": "Primary: model vendor's own docs, launch post or system card.",
    "B": "Benchmark owner or serious independent evaluator (Artificial Analysis, benchmark leaderboards).",
    "C": "Blogs, forums, aggregators, or figures this repo carried forward without re-verification. Signal only; never the sole basis of a rule."
  },
  "comparability_groups": {
    "anthropic-launch-2026-09-01": "Anthropic's Fable 5.1 launch note. One vendor's harness across all listed models, including competitors. Internally comparable; vendor_run true.",
